sandbox. Once a week the whole record is published here as files: what each server advertised, and every change, field by field. Free under CC BY 4.0.\n\n## Latest snapshot: 2026-11-02\n\nFile  | Rows  | Size  | What\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n`servers.jsonl.gz`  | 96,923  | 21.2 MB  | One row per listed server: endpoint, transport, status, tool count, the digest of its current tool list.\n`toolsets.jsonl.gz`  | 90,641  | 1,053.9 MB  | Every tool list a server served (name, description and schemas, as served), current ones and every one a change replaced.\n`changes.jsonl.gz`  | 53,159  | 56.5 MB  | Every recorded change: tools added, removed and modified, field by field, with the signed label.\n`scans.jsonl.gz`  | 11,069  | 754 kB  | WARDEN pattern matches per tool list (rules in pattern-set.json). Leads to read, not verdicts.\n`classifications.jsonl.gz`  | 4,195  | 233 kB  | Advisory LLM readings of tool lists. Not reproducible, so never in the signed log.\n`tool_extras.jsonl.gz`  | 95,178  | 40.6 MB  | What each tool carried beyond those: annotations (readOnlyHint, destructiveHint…), _meta, title, icons. Since 2026-10-22.\n`extras_changes.jsonl.gz`  | 74,812  | 8.0 MB  | Every change to those members, annotation by annotation, with the tools that dropped readOnlyHint.\n`package_observations.jsonl.gz`  | 171,834  | 15.2 MB  | Every run of an npm/PyPI package with the version it ran and the list it served. Versions since 2026-10-26.\n`manifest.json`  |  |  | Counts and SHA-256 of every file, signed by the log's key, with the tree head of the snapshot.\n`README.md`  |  |  | The dataset card: fields, loading, citation, what the data does not say.\n\nNew here? Start with `servers.jsonl.gz` (one row per listed server) and `changes.jsonl.gz` (one row per recorded change, field by field); `toolsets.jsonl.gz` is the large one — every distinct tool list in full. Sizes are in the table.\n\nThe same files: Hugging Face (one tag per snapshot) · Zenodo (a DOI per archived snapshot; the record names its date, and latest/ here may be newer) · latest/ always points at the newest snapshot.\n\n## Load it\n    \n    from datasets import load_dataset   # Hugging Face, any snapshot tag\n    changes = load_dataset(\"alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions\", data_files=\"changes.jsonl.gz\", split=\"train\")\n    \n    -- DuckDB: the servers whose tool lists changed most often\n    SELECT s.name, count(*) AS changes\n    FROM 'https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/changes.jsonl.gz' c\n    JOIN 'https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/servers.jsonl.gz' s ON s.id = c.serverId\n    GROUP BY s.name ORDER BY changes DESC LIMIT 20;\n    \n    import pandas as pd\n    servers = pd.read_json(\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/latest/servers.jsonl.gz\", lines=True)\n\n## Cite\n\nArtamokhov, A. (2026). HISTOR snapshot 2026-11-02: MCP tool definitions and how they change [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23884408\n\nCite the snapshot you counted on: the same query gives other numbers on another snapshot. doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512759 stands for all of them and always opens the newest.\n\n## Check it\n\n`manifest.json` lists the SHA-256 of every file and is signed (Ed25519) by the log's key `did:key:z6Mkw1CVxsPj9utYp7VXWEbuuGM9Ev47itwKu1UfKd5ByxR9`, with the signed tree head the snapshot was taken under. Any label in it can be proven against the live log: https://histor.modelmarket.dev. Code: https://github.com/alexar76/histor.\n\n## All snapshots\n\n  * 2026-11-02 · 90,863 servers · 53,159 changes · doi:10.5281/zenodo.23884408\n  * 2026-10-26 · 85,913 servers · 31,660 changes · doi:10.5281/zenodo.23884119\n  * 2026-10-25 · 85,437 servers · 30,151 changes · doi:10.5281/zenodo.23881379\n  * 2026-10-20 · 81,879 servers · 23,821 changes · doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512760\n\n## What it does not say\n\n  * A tool list is what a server showed an anonymous client on that day; servers that need a key show less or nothing.\n  * A change is a 